Thanks @william8545 ! Agree to your proposal to use a GNMI client cert on the BMC end. This enables us to use certificate to create a mTLS sessions with Switch-Host. We can have a new config something line below 
```
    "GNMI_CLIENT": {
        "certs": {
            "ca_crt": "/etc/sonic/credential/<root>",
            "client_crt": "/etc/sonic/credential/gnmi_client.cer",
            "client_key": "/etc/sonic/credential/gnmi_client.key"
        },  
        "gnmi": {
            "log_level": "2"
        }   
    },  
```
let me know your thoughts

@tahmed-dev, thanks. Tentatively yes to option 1: EVPN-MH devices sync MACs over FPM, and kernel mode stays for single-homed EVPN.

We run kernel-mode EVPN-MH today, so before we commit we'll qualify the FPM path on hardware: #4857 together with this PR and the CLI in sonic-net/sonic-utilities#4833, on Broadcom TH5 and Q3D, covering our EVPN-MH cases including ES peer sync and peer restarts. We'll follow up here with the results.

Until then, could sonic-net/sonic-linux-kernel#619, and the removal of the `proto hw` tag in #4857, wait? Kernel-mode EVPN-MH relies on both, and we need a working path while we move over.
